267873129807413, "served": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"]}], "probes": {"instruction_present": true, "activation_present": true}, "side": false, "subagent": false, "provider": null, "requested": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "served": {"claude-sonnet-5-5": 1}, "parameters": {"max_tokens": 128000, "output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1340, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1340, "cached_input": 49585, "input": 50927, "output": 157}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 62976, "other": 423, "system": 35085, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 40884}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 153765}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "b037a559-4f01-520d-beac-05a5bf5c20cc", "at": 1795682165.182614, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 54503, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b4b81281eb6d5dc27a47dcbb83ff65cf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "a950f0eb-2bd5-5bdf-a2c2-bacf3dbe80b6", "at": 1795682165.1846812, "until": 1795682166.810766, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 54504, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b4b81281eb6d5dc27a47dcbb83ff65cf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_013iqTJ2FXgPAx2dakwDCCBq", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/storywiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git && git pull -q && git log --oneline | head -3; git diff 6bc3e8d HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1800 | tail -n +1 | head -40", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/storywiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git && git pull -q && git log --oneline | head -3; git diff 6bc3e8d HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1800 | tail -n +1 | head -40"]], "output": "```console\n7b5b822 Outline rev 12: paired inner50 interval, ridge counter-case\nc5feb52 Outline rev 11: headline names source-informed balanced+calibration, class-level selection, inner50 move with intervals\n6bc3e8d Outline rev 10: results from analysis (LOBO-selected classes, 2%, inner50, source count)\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-- **Headline (extrapolation, n = 100; selected representatives, leave-one-benchmark-out (LOBO), RMSE ratio to uniform, geometric mean over benchmarks):** *source models help most when the target resembles them. In interpolation and lineage every method class beats uniform sampling (0.65–0.72 of uniform's RMSE for the classes that use sources well, 0.80–0.94 of stratified's). For targets above the sources the gain over stratified sampling is not shown by difference correction (selected 1.03 of strat; post-hoc best 0.96), and what survives selection is design-based variance reduction (`balanced|calreg`, 0.77 of uniform, 0.91 of strat); pure IRT predictors lose to sampling by bias.* The gain over stratified sampling in extrapolation is scale-dependent: at 2 % of N the selected classes are 0.88–0.96 of strat (model-based 0.99). The statements are scoped by distance above the sources (extrap10 / extrap / extrap50: difference-corrected 0.74 / 0.87 / 1.01 of uniform).\n+- **Headline (extrapolation, n = 100; selected representatives, leave-one-benchmark-out (LOBO), RMSE ratio to uniform, geometric mean over benchmarks):** *source models help most when the target resembles them. In interpolation and lineage every method class beats uniform sampling (0.65–0.72 of uniform's RMSE for the classes that use sources well, 0.80–0.94 of stratified's). For targets above the sources the gain over stratified sampling is not shown by difference correction (selected 1.03 of strat; post-hoc best 0.96), and the one combination that beats stratified sampling by a visible margin is **source-informed balanced selection with a source-calibrated regression** (`balanced|calreg`: 0.91 [0.89, 0.93] of strat, 0.77 [0.76, 0.79] of uniform); with the plain mean on the same balanced sample it is 0.95 [0.93, 0.97] of strat, and calibrated regression on stratified or uniform samples is worse than their plain mean (1.17 and 1.23 of strat for strat|calreg and uniform|calreg), so the gain needs the pairing; the difference correction (selected 1.03 [0.99, 1.05]; post-hoc 0.96 [0.93, 0.98]) and the pure IRT predictors do not reach it.* Sources are used in the winning cell (balancing and calibration); the claim is not that sources add nothing in extrapolation. The gain over stratified sampling in extrapolation is scale-dependent: at 2 % of N the selected classes are 0.88–0.96 of strat (model-based 0.99). The statements are scoped by distance above the sources (extrap10 / extrap / extrap50: difference-corrected 0.74 / 0.87 / 1.01 of uniform).\n+- **Open (analysis, host queue):** recal/irtw grid (Brief §3b) and the R = 100 per-target bias run.\n+- **Class-level selection:** LOBO fixes the representative within a class (for the design-based class it picks `balanced|calreg` on every held-out benchmark, 1 distinct choice). Naming that class as the one that beats stratified is a **second, post-hoc step** among five classes on the same targets: the paper shows the whole class table (all five, vs uniform and vs strat, with intervals) and says that 0.91 is the best of the class representatives, not a class chosen by the protocol. The ratio of any two classes (e.g. 0.91 vs 1.03) is read from paired intervals if analysis supplies them, else from the separate intervals, which do not overlap here.\n-- **C2:** the difference estimator removes extrapolation bias with fixed λ = 1; the **tuned λ** is too shrunk in extrapolation when the inner split resembles the sources (`balanced|diff-irt`: tuned 0.815, fixed λ = 1 0.784 at n = 100). With the larger-gap inner split (held-out share 0.5) the tuned one is 0.763, below fixed λ = 1 and below `balanced|calreg` (0.\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "c9d22eff-c66a-599d-ba57-c2fde1b290e1", "at": 1795682166.1859255, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 54519, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b4b81281eb6d5dc27a47dcbb83ff65cf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "0d1b86d5-d5a9-5761-b567-71dd63be6cfe", "at": 1795682166.1879644, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 54520, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b4b81281eb6d5dc27a47dcbb83ff65cf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "153a34bd-fbe1-52b9-afdc-696368bbf3dc", "at": 1795682166.1901903, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 54521, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b4b81281eb6d5dc27a47dcbb83ff65cf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "f0ee53dd-7b35-585f-a963-2fb9decacd2a", "at": 1795682166.278795, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 54525, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authenticat